      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This seems more a problem related to the 'Use two different projects for PC and Quest and just do the same changes' mindset that VRChat advertises when creating cross compatible worlds. \n\nAs such somehow the network ID of two objects are swapped between the platform versions, probably based on the order of the objects in the hierarchy. \n\nThe local cache server is a thing and it speeds up the platform switching process immensely, making two projects not the solution imo.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-04T21:15:43.144Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Cross-platform worlds that feature pickupables (Cafe Leblanc as an example) rarely sync up these objects properly between the PC and Quest versions of the world. While it makes sense for versions to share collisions and networked events, VRC_objectSync in its current state is only reliable in PC-only or Quest-only instances. An ID system for vrc_objectSync (where similar to a world or avatar ID, would generate a code that would be copy-pasted on both the PC and Quest version of the same object) would allow creators to bespokely identify an object between two versions of the same world, so the Quest world doesn't confuse the cup in a PC user's hand as a plate, or vice versa.",
